WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:02.909
- Wait, this is what it's
like when your show has money?

00:00:02.909 --> 00:00:04.218
(audience laughs)

00:00:04.218 --> 00:00:05.451
What?

00:00:05.451 --> 00:00:06.867
There's like, so many lights inside.

00:00:06.867 --> 00:00:08.210
- I love your set, actually.

00:00:08.210 --> 00:00:09.810
That had made me wanna go on your show.

00:00:09.810 --> 00:00:10.643
Are you gonna have

00:00:10.643 --> 00:00:11.476
me on your show?
- Thank you.

00:00:11.476 --> 00:00:12.408
Absolutely!

00:00:12.408 --> 00:00:14.160
My set is the size of my
current greenroom on your stage.

00:00:14.160 --> 00:00:15.230
- You know what, though?

00:00:15.230 --> 00:00:16.886
But that's awesome 'cause
that kind of creates,

00:00:16.886 --> 00:00:18.370
have you done "Andy Cohen Live"?

00:00:18.370 --> 00:00:20.088
Like, it kind of creates
this whole atmosphere

00:00:20.088 --> 00:00:21.700
where you're all together,

00:00:21.700 --> 00:00:22.533
and it creates

00:00:22.533 --> 00:00:23.706
kind of a different vibe.
- Right,

00:00:23.706 --> 00:00:24.539
that's like the nice way.

00:00:24.539 --> 00:00:26.247
That's a nice disclaimer
of being like, "It's small,

00:00:26.247 --> 00:00:27.870
"it's cute, it's intimate."
- No, no!

00:00:27.870 --> 00:00:29.970
I'm being real, 'cause
sometimes on big huge sets,

00:00:29.970 --> 00:00:31.180
it can feel a little cold.

00:00:31.180 --> 00:00:32.470
Like, our job was to warm it up,

00:00:32.470 --> 00:00:33.303
we wanted to warm it up,

00:00:33.303 --> 00:00:35.100
but I actually think
that's really important,

00:00:35.100 --> 00:00:35.933
like about your show.
- Thank you.

00:00:35.933 --> 00:00:38.670
- I think it creates more of
a cozy kind of environment

00:00:38.670 --> 00:00:40.307
to where you really get to open up.

00:00:40.307 --> 00:00:41.140
I love it.
- Well I appreciate that.

00:00:41.140 --> 00:00:41.980
I do love it, don't get me wrong.

00:00:41.980 --> 00:00:43.840
I do love it, it's just my greenroom

00:00:43.840 --> 00:00:46.008
had like chocolates and stuff.
- You're hilarious.

00:00:46.008 --> 00:00:47.714
(both laugh)

00:00:47.714 --> 00:00:49.756
Well, last time we saw each other,

00:00:49.756 --> 00:00:52.350
I think it'd been close to a month.

00:00:52.350 --> 00:00:53.930
'Cause we both started at the same time.

00:00:53.930 --> 00:00:55.960
- I know my sister right here, everybody.

00:00:55.960 --> 00:00:57.230
This is my sister.
- Yes, yes!

00:00:57.230 --> 00:00:59.456
I just need to say, your wins,
- We were texting.

00:00:59.456 --> 00:01:01.950
- Your wins are my wins,
- Agreed.

00:01:01.950 --> 00:01:04.260
- and I'm so happy for you,
and she's doing a great job,

00:01:04.260 --> 00:01:06.980
and it was just so awesome to
be starting at the same time.

00:01:06.980 --> 00:01:07.813
- It really was,

00:01:07.813 --> 00:01:10.070
and it was really nice
to talk to another woman

00:01:10.070 --> 00:01:11.430
that's in a very similar position,

00:01:11.430 --> 00:01:12.390
and just us texting,

00:01:12.390 --> 00:01:14.780
simply was kinda like, very refreshing.

00:01:14.780 --> 00:01:16.060
- I remember texting you one day,

00:01:16.060 --> 00:01:17.820
and I was having a
really overwhelming day,

00:01:17.820 --> 00:01:20.600
and I thought, I bet you
Kelly could relate to this.

00:01:20.600 --> 00:01:21.560
So I picked up the phone,

00:01:21.560 --> 00:01:23.308
and I was like, "My one friend", whatever.

00:01:23.308 --> 00:01:24.141
(Kelly laughs)

00:01:24.141 --> 00:01:26.000
And I was like "Hey, how is it going?"

00:01:26.000 --> 00:01:27.170
And we actually talked about

00:01:27.170 --> 00:01:29.230
how we both just finished crying.

00:01:29.230 --> 00:01:30.190
- Yes, yes.

00:01:30.190 --> 00:01:32.750
That's a normal day that ends
in wine for me, but yeah.

00:01:32.750 --> 00:01:34.640
- And then I always tell you
how I had no time to cry,

00:01:34.640 --> 00:01:36.300
and I had the scheduled 10 minutes to cry,

00:01:36.300 --> 00:01:37.380
because someone kept knocking on my door,

00:01:37.380 --> 00:01:38.297
and I was like, "I'm crying!"

00:01:38.297 --> 00:01:39.730
(audience laughs)
- Yeah, give me a minute!

00:01:39.730 --> 00:01:41.440
- Give me a cry break!

00:01:41.440 --> 00:01:42.990
So it was very refreshing.

00:01:42.990 --> 00:01:45.810
- It is, I think because you
came from YouTube, right?

00:01:45.810 --> 00:01:48.400
And so, what would you
say the difference is?

00:01:48.400 --> 00:01:50.040
Like, because all your YouTube videos,

00:01:50.040 --> 00:01:51.890
and going to now doing
the nighttime thing,

00:01:51.890 --> 00:01:53.460
like, how different is that?

00:01:53.460 --> 00:01:54.293
- Oh, it's so different.

00:01:54.293 --> 00:01:56.820
I mean, on my YouTube
channel I control everything,

00:01:56.820 --> 00:01:59.750
and there's a crew of five
people that work on my content.

00:01:59.750 --> 00:02:01.550
And then I got a show, and y'all,

00:02:01.550 --> 00:02:05.864
there's literally one hundred
people that work on my show.

00:02:05.864 --> 00:02:08.487
There's probably 3000 here,
but 100 work on my show.

00:02:08.487 --> 00:02:10.150
- No, there's about the same. (laughs)

00:02:10.150 --> 00:02:12.650
- And they have all these
jobs that I'm, to be honest,

00:02:12.650 --> 00:02:13.610
not familiar with.

00:02:13.610 --> 00:02:14.443
- Me neither.

00:02:14.443 --> 00:02:15.276
- So, someone will come up
to me, and they'll be like,

00:02:15.276 --> 00:02:17.300
" I'm your script
supervisor", and I'm like.

00:02:17.300 --> 00:02:18.280
And I'm like, "Way to go!"

00:02:18.280 --> 00:02:19.113
(audience laughs)

00:02:19.113 --> 00:02:19.946
- Scripts need supervision?
- Yeah,

00:02:19.946 --> 00:02:20.779
yeah, I know, good job.

00:02:20.779 --> 00:02:21.760
- I don't know what that means.

00:02:21.760 --> 00:02:23.560
- I like the script, so well done.

00:02:23.560 --> 00:02:24.880
- So many names.

00:02:24.880 --> 00:02:25.713
- Yeah, I know.

00:02:25.713 --> 00:02:27.030
- So, I call everyone my friend.

00:02:27.030 --> 00:02:28.950
- It is cool though, how
you have this whole team

00:02:28.950 --> 00:02:30.210
that kind of supports you,

00:02:30.210 --> 00:02:31.043
and like,
- Absolutely.

00:02:31.043 --> 00:02:31.876
- you know, lifts you up,

00:02:31.876 --> 00:02:32.740
and makes your show really awesome.

00:02:32.740 --> 00:02:34.053
I love it, I love having a crew.

00:02:34.053 --> 00:02:35.834
- Late night staff, your talk show staff.

00:02:35.834 --> 00:02:37.554
(audience cheers and applauds)

00:02:37.554 --> 00:02:39.950
The staff really makes it.

00:02:39.950 --> 00:02:42.520
- So, here's my thing with
your new deal, your new life.

00:02:42.520 --> 00:02:43.353
- Okay, talk to me.

00:02:43.353 --> 00:02:46.490
- Have you blown any money on
an indulgence of any sorts?

00:02:46.490 --> 00:02:49.051
- Ooh, well you know, a
lot in my life has changed,

00:02:49.051 --> 00:02:51.663
except for the fact that I'm very cheap.

00:02:51.663 --> 00:02:52.932
(audience laughs)

00:02:52.932 --> 00:02:54.540
And that will be consistent.

00:02:54.540 --> 00:02:56.390
But there is one thing I splurge on.

00:02:56.390 --> 00:02:58.040
I feel like it's very relatable, though.

00:02:58.040 --> 00:03:01.730
The one thing I will splurge
on is birthday parties

00:03:01.730 --> 00:03:02.751
for my dog.

00:03:02.751 --> 00:03:03.740
(audience laughs)

00:03:03.740 --> 00:03:04.960
I will spend

00:03:04.960 --> 00:03:08.791
any amount of money on my dog.
- Does everyone relate?

00:03:08.791 --> 00:03:10.910
She knows what I'm talking
about, she's like (clapping).

00:03:10.910 --> 00:03:11.743
- I mean.

00:03:12.949 --> 00:03:14.820
- She knows what I'm talking about.

00:03:14.820 --> 00:03:15.653
On my dog!

00:03:15.653 --> 00:03:17.060
- Not your birthday.

00:03:17.060 --> 00:03:18.070
Not yours?

00:03:18.070 --> 00:03:20.440
- Listen, on my birthday
I'll be up in a Denny's

00:03:20.440 --> 00:03:22.150
just being casual, okay?

00:03:22.150 --> 00:03:23.370
But my dog's birthday.

00:03:23.370 --> 00:03:24.690
- Moons Over My Hammy.

00:03:24.690 --> 00:03:26.290
- So, he recently turned two.

00:03:26.290 --> 00:03:27.330
I know, they grow up so fast.

00:03:27.330 --> 00:03:28.710
- Mine just turned two.
- Oh really?

00:03:28.710 --> 00:03:29.750
- Henry, yeah.

00:03:29.750 --> 00:03:30.583
- Well, we're the same.

00:03:30.583 --> 00:03:31.730
- Yeah, we're the same human.

00:03:31.730 --> 00:03:32.670
- My dog turned two,

00:03:32.670 --> 00:03:35.259
and I gave him a Harry
Potter themed birthday.

00:03:35.259 --> 00:03:36.160
(audience gasps and applauds)

00:03:36.160 --> 00:03:36.993
- Yes.

00:03:36.993 --> 00:03:38.358
- I love Harry Potter.

00:03:38.358 --> 00:03:39.191
- Yes!

00:03:40.307 --> 00:03:42.730
- "Have you seen this wizard?"

00:03:42.730 --> 00:03:45.640
- And it took place in Dogwarts.

00:03:45.640 --> 00:03:46.733
Thank you, thank you.

00:03:46.733 --> 00:03:49.200
- Thank you, thank you. (laughs)

00:03:49.200 --> 00:03:50.890
- I love Harry Potter as well.

00:03:50.890 --> 00:03:51.850
- I mean, it was great.

00:03:51.850 --> 00:03:53.900
All of his dog friends came.

00:03:53.900 --> 00:03:55.544
I made all these cupcakes.

00:03:55.544 --> 00:03:58.100
Look at him, he's dressed as a Gryffindor.

00:03:58.100 --> 00:03:59.057
I mean, it's just a whole thing.

00:03:59.057 --> 00:04:01.326
It's a whole thing.
- Oh my gosh, I love you.

00:04:01.326 --> 00:04:02.159
- Thank you.

00:04:02.159 --> 00:04:03.830
- That's so cute that you
spend your money on others.

00:04:03.830 --> 00:04:05.740
- Oh, absolutely.
- I do the same, totally.

00:04:05.740 --> 00:04:06.573
(audience laughs)

00:04:06.573 --> 00:04:09.270
- I feel like I have
my priorities in check.

00:04:09.270 --> 00:04:10.103
- Me too.

00:04:10.103 --> 00:04:11.165
- I do.
- Mine are different, though.

00:04:11.165 --> 00:04:13.477
(both laugh)

00:04:13.477 --> 00:04:15.837
- I was like "Happy
birthday, Henry!", snuggle.

00:04:15.837 --> 00:04:17.800
(laughter)

00:04:17.800 --> 00:04:20.220
But you have an awesome
connection with your fans.

00:04:20.220 --> 00:04:21.053
- Yes.

00:04:21.053 --> 00:04:21.886
- And I actually love that about you,

00:04:21.886 --> 00:04:23.330
and I think that's why you're successful.

00:04:23.330 --> 00:04:26.520
And what is, maybe, your most fun,

00:04:26.520 --> 00:04:28.200
or coolest kind of fan encounter?

00:04:28.200 --> 00:04:29.033
- I mean, there's so many.

00:04:29.033 --> 00:04:32.620
I really do genuinely
love my fans so much.

00:04:32.620 --> 00:04:35.070
I mean, when you come
from the digital space,

00:04:35.070 --> 00:04:36.920
you really understand that
there's no record label,

00:04:36.920 --> 00:04:38.840
there was no one that's started

00:04:38.840 --> 00:04:40.420
except for people just
supporting you online.

00:04:40.420 --> 00:04:42.608
So those supporters are really responsible

00:04:42.608 --> 00:04:44.130
for a lot of what I have,

00:04:44.130 --> 00:04:45.580
and so I have so much love for them.

00:04:45.580 --> 00:04:48.340
But one of the most
meaningful stories I think,

00:04:48.340 --> 00:04:52.380
you know, earlier this year
when I came out online,

00:04:52.380 --> 00:04:54.180
I remember I was really scared,

00:04:54.180 --> 00:04:56.520
and it was before I had a trip to India.

00:04:56.520 --> 00:04:58.590
And, you know, Indian
culture is quite taboo

00:04:58.590 --> 00:04:59.490
when it comes to sexuality,

00:04:59.490 --> 00:05:00.680
and I was so stressed going to India,

00:05:00.680 --> 00:05:02.320
and I was like " Oh, what
are people gonna think?"

00:05:02.320 --> 00:05:03.153
I don't know.

00:05:03.153 --> 00:05:04.600
And I had a meet and greet,

00:05:04.600 --> 00:05:05.990
and I met with 200 fans,

00:05:05.990 --> 00:05:09.080
and honestly, I'd say about a hundred fans

00:05:09.080 --> 00:05:11.450
came out to me, to my face,
during that meet and greet.

00:05:11.450 --> 00:05:13.700
And for me, that was so powerful, because,

00:05:13.700 --> 00:05:15.690
one, I know how hard that is,

00:05:15.690 --> 00:05:18.020
and I was like wow, me being myself

00:05:18.020 --> 00:05:18.853
did something for you.
- And you inspired them

00:05:18.853 --> 00:05:20.477
to be confident enough to say it.

00:05:20.477 --> 00:05:21.310
(audience applauds)
- And what better legacy,

00:05:21.310 --> 00:05:22.143
you know, so,

00:05:22.143 --> 00:05:23.584
that was pretty cool.
- That's the coolest.

00:05:23.584 --> 00:05:24.825
- Thank you, thank you.

